1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,560
This is Basil.

2
00:00:01,860 --> 00:00:03,900
Basil is sitting in an ice box.

3
00:00:05,077 --> 00:00:06,167
Yep, that's me.

4
00:00:06,537 --> 00:00:08,787
You're probably wondering how I got here.

5
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:10,024
Basil!

6
00:00:10,384 --> 00:00:13,174
Your race with Uncle Lim starts in three minutes!

7
00:00:13,528 --> 00:00:16,628
And your bike has no bell, no chain and no brakes!

8
00:00:17,127 --> 00:00:18,756
Because LIGHTER IS FASTER!

9
00:00:19,103 --> 00:00:21,773
Basil is not an expert at bicycles.

10
00:00:22,692 --> 00:00:24,422
The Great Void Deck Race!

11
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:25,879
Three minutes!

12
00:00:26,149 --> 00:00:28,199
Which fix gets Basil racing?

13
00:00:28,551 --> 00:00:30,051
Fix one: no fixing.

14
00:00:30,351 --> 00:00:31,921
I just pedal faster!

15
00:00:32,267 --> 00:00:34,487
Fix two: put all three parts back.

16
00:00:34,937 --> 00:00:36,477
I made a checklist.

17
00:00:36,828 --> 00:00:38,448
You always make a checklist.

18
00:00:38,795 --> 00:00:40,385
And you never read it.

19
00:00:40,739 --> 00:00:43,429
Fix three: put the chain and the brakes back, and skip the

20
00:00:43,449 --> 00:00:44,059
bell.

21
00:00:44,349 --> 00:00:46,079
A bell can't make you go!

22
00:00:46,575 --> 00:00:48,715
Show me one, two or three fingers!

23
00:00:57,383 --> 00:00:58,594
Team high-five!

24
00:01:00,113 --> 00:01:01,253
Let's test them!

25
00:01:01,533 --> 00:01:03,553
But first: ten minutes earlier...

26
00:01:05,123 --> 00:01:07,863
Uncle Lim's old bike is full of useless parts.

27
00:01:08,253 --> 00:01:09,283
Mine won't be.

28
00:01:09,703 --> 00:01:11,083
LIGHTER IS FASTER!

29
00:01:11,318 --> 00:01:12,288
Who needs a bell?

30
00:01:12,688 --> 00:01:14,048
I'm faster as well!

31
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:14,920
Um...

32
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:17,130
but what does THAT part do?

33
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,430
It goes ring.

34
00:01:18,779 --> 00:01:19,749
That's all.

35
00:01:20,097 --> 00:01:21,666
But WHY does it go ring?

36
00:01:22,017 --> 00:01:23,177
Nobody knows.

37
00:01:23,447 --> 00:01:24,557
Off it comes!

38
00:01:27,213 --> 00:01:28,193
Ring, ring!

39
00:01:30,356 --> 00:01:33,476
A bell warns people, and pigeons, that you are coming.

40
00:01:33,926 --> 00:01:35,996
Basil is not an expert at bells.

41
00:01:36,653 --> 00:01:38,213
I have made some new friends.

42
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:40,095
Who needs a chain?

43
00:01:40,455 --> 00:01:41,865
It's a greasy pain!

44
00:01:42,211 --> 00:01:42,981
Um...

45
00:01:44,861 --> 00:01:46,321
It goes round and round.

46
00:01:46,601 --> 00:01:47,561
That's all.

47
00:01:47,909 --> 00:01:49,879
But WHY does it go round and round?

48
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:51,808
To make my tail greasy.

49
00:01:52,168 --> 00:01:53,268
Off it comes!

50
00:01:55,531 --> 00:01:58,701
Without a chain, the pedals cannot turn the back wheel.

51
00:02:01,524 --> 00:02:03,544
The slowest overtake in history.

52
00:02:03,814 --> 00:02:06,064
Let's see it again, in slow motion.

53
00:02:08,728 --> 00:02:10,918
Basil, you just lost to a snail.

54
00:02:11,271 --> 00:02:12,521
Because it's LIGHTER!

55
00:02:13,319 --> 00:02:14,229
To the ramp!

56
00:02:14,499 --> 00:02:15,639
Who needs brakes?

57
00:02:15,949 --> 00:02:17,409
Speed is all it takes!

58
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:18,532
Um...

59
00:02:20,352 --> 00:02:21,572
What they said.

60
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:23,139
Brakes slow you down.

61
00:02:23,519 --> 00:02:25,059
Winners never slow down!

62
00:02:25,409 --> 00:02:27,789
But WHY would anybody want to slow down?

63
00:02:28,137 --> 00:02:29,087
Exactly!

64
00:02:29,377 --> 00:02:30,507
Off they come!

65
00:02:33,092 --> 00:02:34,092
The bike!

66
00:02:34,482 --> 00:02:35,902
It's rolling away!

67
00:02:38,285 --> 00:02:39,175
Basil!

68
00:02:39,595 --> 00:02:40,985
Squeeze the brakes!

69
00:02:41,033 --> 00:02:42,573
It hasn't GOT any brakes!

70
00:02:42,629 --> 00:02:44,969
Then nothing can slow its wheels down.

71
00:02:45,419 --> 00:02:46,729
It can't stop!

72
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:49,050
We need something big to stop it!

73
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:50,639
The ice box!

74
00:02:53,701 --> 00:02:56,391
Brakes help a bike slow down and stop safely.

75
00:02:56,671 --> 00:02:57,991
Basil is fine.

76
00:02:58,291 --> 00:03:00,021
Basil is a little cold.

77
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:02,030
Don't do this at home.

78
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:03,660
Seriously.

79
00:03:04,534 --> 00:03:05,614
In a world...

80
00:03:05,844 --> 00:03:08,224
where one lizard thought a bell was too heavy...

81
00:03:08,444 --> 00:03:10,334
one race decides everything.

82
00:03:12,989 --> 00:03:14,129
Helmets on.

83
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,119
Ready, steady, GO!

84
00:03:21,434 --> 00:03:23,264
Slowly, slowly.

85
00:03:25,121 --> 00:03:26,431
Was that the bike?

86
00:03:26,482 --> 00:03:27,172
Yes.

87
00:03:27,716 --> 00:03:28,626
I let him win.

88
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:31,011
Your bike didn't even move.

89
00:03:31,357 --> 00:03:32,647
I let it not move.

90
00:03:33,115 --> 00:03:36,875
Basil's pedals turn, but nothing joins them to the back wheel.

91
00:03:37,125 --> 00:03:40,015
Pedalling faster cannot do the chain's job.

92
00:03:40,829 --> 00:03:43,089
But WHY did the old, heavy bike win?

93
00:03:43,819 --> 00:03:46,069
Look closer at Uncle Lim's bike.

94
00:03:46,415 --> 00:03:48,835
His bell warns people that he is coming.

95
00:03:49,195 --> 00:03:51,395
His brakes slow him down at the corner.

96
00:03:51,975 --> 00:03:54,755
And his chain turns the back wheel when he pedals!

97
00:03:55,326 --> 00:03:58,836
Every part has its own special job, called its function.

98
00:04:00,304 --> 00:04:02,764
So my useless parts all had functions.

99
00:04:03,112 --> 00:04:04,832
I told you s...

100
00:04:05,031 --> 00:04:06,612
Nice try, Basil.

101
00:04:06,964 --> 00:04:10,514
His bike is heavier, but it won, because all its parts work

102
00:04:10,534 --> 00:04:11,274
together.

103
00:04:12,005 --> 00:04:13,095
Sorry, bike.

104
00:04:14,625 --> 00:04:16,964
Be one little link of Uncle Lim's chain!

105
00:04:17,245 --> 00:04:18,235
Shrink down.

106
00:04:18,505 --> 00:04:19,435
Quietly.

107
00:04:21,301 --> 00:04:24,901
The front gear's teeth fit into your gaps, and pull you forward.

108
00:04:25,681 --> 00:04:28,881
The whole chain moves, and tugs the back gear round.

109
00:04:29,688 --> 00:04:31,198
The back wheel turns!

110
00:04:32,938 --> 00:04:35,428
Pedals, front gear, chain, back gear, wheel.

111
00:04:35,838 --> 00:04:37,648
Each part acts on the next one.

112
00:04:37,988 --> 00:04:40,158
Scientists say the parts interact.

113
00:04:41,515 --> 00:04:42,385
Okay.

114
00:04:42,665 --> 00:04:44,205
I want my parts back.

115
00:04:45,303 --> 00:04:46,713
Every part has a job.

116
00:04:47,073 --> 00:04:48,303
Brakes, stop me.

117
00:04:48,643 --> 00:04:49,893
No more mistakes!

118
00:04:51,135 --> 00:04:52,545
Every part has a job.

119
00:04:52,885 --> 00:04:54,515
Chain, turn my wheel again!

120
00:04:56,088 --> 00:04:57,208
Chain and brakes!

121
00:04:57,688 --> 00:04:59,248
That's my fix three!

122
00:04:59,558 --> 00:05:00,688
Race time!

123
00:05:01,594 --> 00:05:02,094
Wait.

124
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:03,885
Checklist.

125
00:05:04,274 --> 00:05:05,474
Ring the bell.

126
00:05:05,828 --> 00:05:06,818
Ring, ring?

127
00:05:07,130 --> 00:05:08,230
Quick question!

128
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,800
Without a bell, can the bike still move?

129
00:05:11,090 --> 00:05:12,230
Think about it.

130
00:05:15,893 --> 00:05:18,303
It can still move, but it is not as safe!

131
00:05:18,656 --> 00:05:19,426
Yes!

132
00:05:19,696 --> 00:05:22,996
When one part stops working, the whole bike is likely to be

133
00:05:23,016 --> 00:05:23,816
affected.

134
00:05:24,663 --> 00:05:26,073
Every part has a job.

135
00:05:26,393 --> 00:05:27,633
Bell, you warn them well!

136
00:05:29,727 --> 00:05:32,287
So a system is made up of different parts...

137
00:05:32,343 --> 00:05:34,473
...each part has its own function...

138
00:05:34,531 --> 00:05:36,022
...and the parts interact.

139
00:05:36,311 --> 00:05:37,772
My bike is a system!

140
00:05:39,188 --> 00:05:40,798
ALL PARTS, WORKING TOGETHER!

141
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:46,150
Basil, you're puffing!

142
00:05:46,541 --> 00:05:47,550
But WHY?

143
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:48,900
Look closer.

144
00:05:49,490 --> 00:05:51,911
Your bones and muscles move your legs.

145
00:05:52,481 --> 00:05:55,421
Your heart beats faster, and you breathe faster.

146
00:05:55,990 --> 00:05:58,400
Your body is made up of systems too.

147
00:06:00,077 --> 00:06:01,967
And the rain tree is a system.

148
00:06:02,427 --> 00:06:05,317
Its roots, stem and leaves each have a function.

149
00:06:06,347 --> 00:06:08,747
Now, here are the words that earn marks.

150
00:06:08,804 --> 00:06:09,964
Say it with me!

151
00:06:10,672 --> 00:06:12,892
A system is made up of different parts.

152
00:06:13,172 --> 00:06:14,902
Each part has its own function.

153
00:06:15,192 --> 00:06:17,372
The parts interact to perform a function.

154
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:21,082
When one part stops working, the whole system is likely to be

155
00:06:21,102 --> 00:06:22,032
affected.

156
00:06:24,505 --> 00:06:25,485
But wait.

157
00:06:25,765 --> 00:06:27,505
Somebody is still racing!

158
00:06:27,825 --> 00:06:29,187
Go, snail, go!

159
00:06:31,687 --> 00:06:33,467
Slowly, slowly.

160
00:06:33,837 --> 00:06:35,657
Every part working.

161
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:38,840
Picked fix two?

162
00:06:39,110 --> 00:06:41,040
You win a point, and so does Pip!

163
00:06:41,690 --> 00:06:43,890
Let's read today's key words together!

164
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:44,940
Ready?

165
00:06:45,227 --> 00:06:46,107
Function.

166
00:06:47,411 --> 00:06:48,261
Interact.

167
00:06:49,799 --> 00:06:50,639
System.

168
00:06:52,010 --> 00:06:52,950
Well done!

169
00:06:53,932 --> 00:06:55,033
Say it with us!

170
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:56,583
Ready?

171
00:06:56,706 --> 00:06:57,366
One!

172
00:06:57,706 --> 00:06:58,406
two!

173
00:06:58,711 --> 00:06:59,886
Now you know!

174
00:07:04,896 --> 00:07:06,206
LIGHTER IS FAST...

175
00:07:07,117 --> 00:07:08,256
I'll keep the bell.

176
00:07:08,276 --> 00:07:09,416
Take two!
